<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="extra-time-penalties" data-rev="2">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> content/rules/default.json, data/rules.rs, content/README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Rule pack schema 4 with an extra_time block (two 15-minute periods, 300 seconds of added time at most, one extra substitution, one extra window) and a shootout block (five kicks, a 10-round allowance).</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>data</td><td>+106 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> rules/clock.rs, rules/mod.rs, rules/restart.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The clock moves from halves to periods, so minute 105 reads 105. A level knockout match opens an extra-time break through the half-time path with no energy recovery. A level extra time starts the shoot-out: one penalty dead ball per kick on the pitch, the others in the centre circle, each kick ending on a goal, a save, the ball leaving play or stopping, or 5 seconds of live ball.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>rules</td><td>+250 / -44</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> rules/shootout.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure law functions: eligible kickers with numbers equalised, the shoot-out keeper, kicker order, alternation, the early decision, sudden death, and a 100-round safety cap.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>rules</td><td>+240</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> decision.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The open-play shot code becomes shot_kick(), called unchanged by the carrier decision and always by the shoot-out taker. Draw order unchanged.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine</td><td>+20 / -14</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> tactics/change.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The substitution limit and window count rise by the rule pack's extra-time values once the clock is in extra time; nothing applies during the shoot-out.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tactics</td><td>+25 / -4</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> sim.rs, snapshot.rs, observe/mod.rs, commentary/mod.rs, scenario.rs, rng.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Knockout switch off by default; announced maximum 530,000 ticks for a 90-minute knockout match; shoot-out state in snapshot version 4; extra-time and shoot-out statistics as additive extras; no award line for shoot-out kicks; test scene methods; the coin tosses.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine</td><td>+244 / -11</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol event.rs, message.rs, lib.rs, docs/reference/protocol.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Optional fields on existing events; no new event type; no version raised by this slice; the knockout meaning of the announced length documented.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>protocol</td><td>+83 / -2</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">service</span> engine-cli cli.rs, simulate.rs, bench.rs, serve.rs, record.rs, stream_run.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A --knockout flag on the commands that build a match; the stream loop keeps going through a long sudden death.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>cli</td><td>+36 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/history.mjs, web/main.mjs, web/tests/history.test.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">The scrubber maximum follows the newest tick when a match runs past its announced length; history growth already exists.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web</td><td>+26 / -1</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> tests/rules_extra_time.rs, rules_shootout.rs (new); fatigue.rs, content.rs, snapshot.rs (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">A forced draw runs extra time and an on-pitch shoot-out to one winner; the sixth substitution applies in extra time and a seventh is rejected; energy never jumps at minute 90; snapshots resume through extra time and from a shoot-out kick.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>tests</td><td>+570 / -2</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · A shoot-out kick never ends</div><div class="callout-body">Only the defending keeper may gain the ball, a 5-second live cap ends each kick, and a 100-round safety cap ends a runaway shoot-out with an error signal.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · A missed field breaks resume</div><div class="callout-body">Every shoot-out kick is a stoppage with a snapshot; version 4 stores the shoot-out state, and two continuation tests guard it.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · The default match changes by accident</div><div class="callout-body">Tosses only when extra time and the shoot-out start; the shot extraction keeps the draw order; the unchanged determinism test is the gate.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · Sudden death runs past the announced maximum</div><div class="callout-body">Accepted by the product owner; the page history grows, the scrubber follows, and the stream loop continues during the shoot-out.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · Knockout matches are longer</div><div class="callout-body">At most 530,000 announced ticks, about 50 MB of page history, only when --knockout is set.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>2 prior revisions</summary><ul><li><a href="history/04-plan-extra-time-penalties-0.md">rev 0</a> (2026-09-22): first plan; Q-1 opened.</li><li><a href="history/04-plan-extra-time-penalties-1.md">rev 1</a> (2026-09-23): auto-review after the tactics slice landed; Q-1 still open.</li></ul></details>
